{"id": "EUVD-2026-76488", "enisaUuid": "a08e8260-e277-3026-875b-44787bdde484", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-era: fix shadowed superblock leak on take-snap failure\n\nmetadata_take_snap() bumps the live superblock refcount and then\ndm_tm_shadow_block() allocates a new block for the metadata snapshot.\nIf the subsequent dm_sm_inc_block() of writeset_tree_root or\nera_array_root fails, the function only unlocks the clone and\nreturns.  The newly allocated shadow block is never returned to the\nmetadata space map, so each failed take-snap permanently leaks one\nmetadata block.\n\nFree the clone with dm_sm_dec_block() on those error paths, matching\nthe final step of metadata_drop_snap().", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54dd21ca945ecc07885012b9f3e8197f091cfba0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef00efb6fcaee88f50891279ceced17c614e97f7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9fa68b89214bc65af0ef963af7ec3cce9f866e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc731d7fddfd6149f5e88ea080475d18c36d3c64", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d66ceeefb87ddb097b0546bafc581380b816b048", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36ff918637e3517f732188a3c39dbeae5b9cfb1b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6876ca330e741fb8886d12070cb6a7f9cb67257e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39c5aa3bd8ec3912d2cd0b3fe092642b0d2b0713"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89576", "GHSA-f7fr-q69f-62x9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0022e3f8-88fc-33d9-b2fd-d238350302c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "05c06d31-3e98-30fc-84f8-c8ad077b6d85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "06845798-56a3-31d2-a0ea-32b0e39d7254", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "